.TH snip-keys 5 "" "snip 0.6.0" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-keys \- snip TUI key binding format
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
keys.toml customizes rebindable TUI actions by mode. Run snip keys path to locate it, snip keys export to create a complete authoritative starting point, snip keys list to inspect the effective map, and snip keys check after editing.
.SH "FILE FORMAT"
The top\-level inherit\-defaults boolean defaults to true. Each configurable mode is a TOML table whose keys are action slugs and whose values are one chord string or a list of chord strings. An explicit empty list unbinds an action. A complete export sets inherit\-defaults = false.
.RS 4
.nf
inherit\-defaults = true
.fi
.RE
.RS 4
.nf
[list]
"snippet.edit\-content" = "e"
"snippet.rename" = ["r", "f2"]
"snippet.move" = []
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mentioned actions lose their previous bindings before replacements are inserted, allowing two keys to be swapped. Duplicate claims in one mode are rejected together. ctrl\-c is reserved. Unknown modes, action slugs, chord names, and configurable search mode entries are errors.
.SH "MODES"
Normal pane stacks include global and the focused pane mode. Exclusive fragment\-grab, trash, help, git, gist, and search modes take over input but inherit a small allowlist from global. When several modes are active, the narrower mode wins.
.PP
Configurable modes are global, sidebar, list, preview, fragment, fragment\-grab, trash, help, git, and gist. Search text editing, digits, ctrl\-c, and mouse gestures are fixed rather than rebindable.
.SH "GLOBAL DEFAULTS"
/ searches the library. : or ctrl\-p opens the command palette. ? toggles help. A cycles appearance. N toggles line numbers. S toggles the sidebar. T toggles trash. Y copies the snippet ID. [ and ] select preview items. h/l or arrows move across panes. p copies a managed path. q quits. s cycles sort. y copies content. z toggles density. { and } jump paragraphs. Tab and shift\-tab change pane. Esc dismisses. F5 or ctrl\-r rescans. ctrl\-g and ctrl\-s toggle Git and Gist panels.
.SH "SIDEBAR DEFAULTS"
j/k and arrows move, g/G or Home/End jump, ctrl\-d/ctrl\-u page, Space expands folders, Enter applies a filter, n creates a folder, r renames, m moves, and d deletes the selected empty folder or tag.
.SH "LIST AND PREVIEW DEFAULTS"
j/k, g/G, and paging keys navigate. n creates a snippet; e edits content; E edits a note; R edits README; r renames; t edits tags; m moves; d trashes; f changes language; P toggles pin; L toggles lock; v opens the selected fragment; Enter enters preview.
.PP
Preview additionally uses \- and = to collapse or expand fragments. Drag selects preview text and mouse\-up copies it.
.SH "FRAGMENT DEFAULTS"
When the fragment tree is expanded, n adds, r renames, m grabs for reordering, and d removes. While a fragment is grabbed, j/k chooses the destination, Enter drops, and Esc cancels. ctrl\-g and ctrl\-s remain inherited.
.SH "TRASH DEFAULTS"
j/k, g/G, and paging keys navigate. u or Enter restores. x permanently purges. q or Esc closes trash. T, ctrl\-g, ctrl\-s, and the command palette remain inherited.
.SH "HELP DEFAULTS"
/ filters help, a switches current/all scope, s changes sorting, j/k moves, braces or ctrl\-u/ctrl\-d page, and q or Esc closes help. ?, ctrl\-g, ctrl\-s, and the command palette remain inherited.
.SH "GIT DEFAULTS"
ctrl\-g toggles the panel. c commits, C supplies a message, b backs up, p pushes, f fetches, l pulls, r refreshes, i initializes or changes interval, u toggles auto\-push, U toggles startup auto\-pull, o toggles backup\-on\-quit, and a pauses automatic backup for the session.
.SH "GIST DEFAULTS"
ctrl\-s toggles the panel. p publishes or updates a secret gist, P publishes publicly, a attaches, d detaches, o opens a browser, r verifies the remote, x deletes, and y copies the URL.
.SH "FIXED INPUTS"
Search accepts printable characters, Backspace, Enter, and Esc. Digits 1 through 9 and 0 jump to the first through tenth visible item where supported. The mouse wheel scrolls the hovered pane, click selects, double\-click drills into preview, drag selects text, and mouse\-up copies selected preview text.
